# Fitness Application – End-to-End Azure Architecture Implementation Guide

## Architecture Overview

The Fitness Application is designed using Azure cloud-native services with a secure, scalable, and highly available architecture.

```text
Users
   |
Azure Front Door Premium
   |
Application Gateway (WAF v2)
   |
Azure App Service
   |
Production Slot
   |
Green Slot
   |
Azure Cosmos DB (Mongo API)
```

---

# Phase 1 – Network Foundation

## Create Resource Group

```text
RG-FitnessApp-Prod
```

Purpose:

* Logical container for all Azure resources.

---

## Create Virtual Network

```text
vnet-fitness-prod
```

Purpose:

* Provides private networking between resources.

---

## Create Subnets

### Application Gateway Subnet

```text
snet-appgateway
```

Purpose:

* Dedicated subnet for Application Gateway.

---

### App Service Integration Subnet

```text
snet-appservice-integration
```

Purpose:

* Used for App Service VNet Integration.

---

### Private Endpoint Subnet

```text
snet-private-endpoints
```

Purpose:

* Hosts all private endpoints.

---

# Phase 2 – Secrets Management

## Create Azure Key Vault

```text
kv-fitness-prod
```

Store:

```text
Mongo Connection String
API Keys
JWT Secrets
Application Secrets
```

---

## Enable Managed Identity

Enable:

```text
System Assigned Managed Identity
```

for:

```text
fitness-app-prod
```

Grant:

```text
Key Vault Secrets User
```

permission to App Service.

Flow:

```text
App Service
    |
Managed Identity
    |
Key Vault
    |
Secrets
```

---

# Phase 3 – Database Layer

## Create Cosmos DB

Service:

```text
Azure Cosmos DB for MongoDB
```

Name:

```text
cosmos-fitness-prod
```

Purpose:

* Store users
* Store workouts
* Store nutrition plans
* Store application data

---

## Create Private Endpoint

```text
pe-cosmos-fitness-prod
```

Subnet:

```text
snet-private-endpoints
```

Purpose:

* Remove public database access.

---

## Create Private DNS Zone

```text
privatelink.mongo.cosmos.azure.com
```

Link DNS Zone to:

```text
vnet-fitness-prod
```

Purpose:

* Resolve Cosmos DB hostname to private IP.

---

# Phase 4 – Application Layer

## Create App Service Plan

```text
asp-fitness-prod
```

Runtime:

```text
Node.js 22 LTS
```

---

## Create App Service

```text
fitness-app-prod
```

Purpose:

* Host backend APIs
* Host application services

---

## Configure Environment Variables

Add:

```text
MONGO_CONNECTION_STRING

JWT_SECRET

NODE_ENV=production

PORT=8080
```

Future Enhancement:

```text
Key Vault References
```

instead of plain text values.

---

## Configure VNet Integration

Connect:

```text
fitness-app-prod
```

to:

```text
snet-appservice-integration
```

Purpose:

```text
App Service
      |
VNet
      |
Private Endpoint
      |
Cosmos DB
```

---

# Phase 5 – Blue Green Deployment

## Create Deployment Slots

### Green Slot

```text
fitness-app-prod-green
```

Purpose:

* New application release deployment.

---

### Production Slot

```text
fitness-app-prod
```

Purpose:

* Live production traffic.

---

## Deployment Flow

Current:

```text
Production
|
Version 1.0
```

Deploy:

```text
Green
|
Version 2.0
```

Test:

```text
fitness-app-prod-green.azurewebsites.net
```

Swap:

```text
Green -> Production

Production -> Green
```

Benefits:

* Zero downtime deployment
* Instant rollback
* Safe releases

